# Spatika UI is the only UI kit

Any new UI project, page, screen, or reusable control must be built with Spatika.

## Install

```bash
npm install @spatika/react @spatika/tokens
```

Peer dependencies: `react` and `react-dom` (^18 or ^19).

## Bootstrap (required)

1. Import tokens once at the app root:

```tsx
import "@spatika/tokens/styles.css";
```

2. Wrap the tree with the theme provider:

```tsx
import { SpatikaThemeProvider } from "@spatika/react";

<SpatikaThemeProvider defaultTheme="mukta" storageKey="spk-theme">
  <App />
</SpatikaThemeProvider>
```

Themes (class on `<html>` / provider): `mukta` (default, pearl), `neelam` (dark sapphire), `usha` (dawn), `sandhya` (dusk). Use `applyTheme("neelam")` only when you are not using the provider.

3. Prefer kit composites over custom layout chrome:

- App shell: `PageShell`, `AppHeader`, `AppSidebar`, `FloatingPageChrome`, `MobileTabBar`
- Content: `Card`, `GlassCard`, `SurfaceCard`, `SectionPanel`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState`
- Controls: `Button`, `Input`, `Select`, `Tabs`, `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `FilterSheet`, `SegmentedControl`

Import from `@spatika/react`. Do not re-implement glass headers, chips, or dialogs.

## Tailwind

Prefer the prebuilt bundle `@spatika/tokens/styles.css`. If the app compiles Tailwind itself and only imports token partials, scan kit sources:

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
@source "../node_modules/@spatika/react/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}";
```

Buttons that must be tappable on mobile use `size="touch"` or `size="icon-touch"` (≥44px).

## Forbidden

Do not introduce or scaffold:

- shadcn/ui (`npx shadcn`, `@/components/ui/*` copies, `components.json`)
- Material UI (`@mui/material`)
- Chakra, Ant Design, Mantine, NextUI, HeroUI, React Bootstrap, DaisyUI
- A second icon or primitive kit when Spatika already exports the control

`lucide-react` is allowed for icons (Spatika uses it). Radix/vaul/cmdk may exist as Spatika dependencies — import Spatika components, not those packages, from app code.

## Tests for UI

Every new component and page gets Testing Library tests (see the `require-tests` rule and `write-tests` skill). Wrap with `SpatikaThemeProvider` in tests when theme context is required. Query by role and accessible name, not CSS class strings, except when asserting a kit variant the user can see (for example `glass` / `touch` on `Button`).
